reps: 8
vscode: select from the comma to the bracket, Delete
open: notify.ts

@brief
Eight times: remove the third argument and its comma, leaving
`send(customer.email, 'REFUND_SENT');`. Save, quit.

@keys
| `2f,` | onto the second comma |
| `dt)` | delete up to, not including, the closing bracket |

@hints
Park on the comma that should go, then delete up to the bracket.
--
`2f,` then `dt)`.

@solution
    2f, dt) :wq<Enter>

Ten keystrokes, six of them navigation. The reason to drill it is that
the shape — get to the separator with `f`, delete to the terminator with
`t` — is the same shape whether the line is an argument list, an import,
an array literal or a CSS rule. Different characters, identical gesture.

@start notify.ts
await this.emailService.send(customer.email, 'REFUND_SENT', order.id);

@expected notify.ts
await this.emailService.send(customer.email, 'REFUND_SENT');
